course: dictionary
lesson: 4100
title: Old words, kind words
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words were once normal but are now unkind. «Gipsy» is an old word for the Romani people, who came to Europe from India long ago. Many Romani and Traveller people find «gipsy» rude, especially when it is used as an insult. Today it is kinder to say Roma, Romani people or Travellers.
explain: Some families still call themselves Gipsies or Gypsies with pride, so the best rule is to listen to how people describe themselves. Words can also be spelt in different ways, such as gipsy and gypsy, but the spelling does not change how the word can hurt.
explain: Old books show old ideas. In «The Wind in the Willows», the word is used as it was in Edwardian times, with unfair ideas about a whole people. When you read it, you do not copy those ideas. You name them as wrong today, and you can still enjoy the story.
fact: «Gipsy» is an old word for a member of the Romani people.
fact: Romani people have their own language, called Romani, and a long history in Europe.
fact: Many Romani and Traveller people find «gipsy» rude, especially when it is used as an insult.
fact: Judging a whole people by an old idea, such as «they all love horse-dealing», is unfair.
fact: The word «gipsy» is still used in some names, like the gipsy moth, and in «gipsy caravan».
exercise: The dictionary says «gipsy» is an old word for which people? | *Romani people | Sailors | People who ride horses | Scottish people
exercise: Which name is kinder to use today for Romani people? | *Roma, Romani people or Travellers | Gypsy, said as an insult | A gipsy moth | Gipsy
exercise: «The book calls the man a «gipsy» and says gipsies were «very fond of horse-dealing».» Is it fair to say all gipsies love horse-dealing? | Yes, but only in Edwardian times | *No, that is an unfair old idea, not a fact | Only some gipsies do | Yes, it is a fact because the book says so
test: Why is the word «gipsy» better avoided today? | Because it is too long to spell | Because it means dangerous | Because it is a Scottish word | *Because many Romani and Traveller people find it rude
test: Where does the word appear in a name, with no insult meant? | A washerwoman | A steam engine | *The gipsy moth | Toad's horse
exam: Which is the best way to write about Romani people today? | Say all gipsies are good with horses | *Say Roma, Romani people or Travellers, and name old unfair ideas as wrong | Use gipsy for everyone, because old books do | Avoid the topic completely and never mention them
